  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mini-grids serving vulnerable households</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Foundation Rural Energy Services (FRES) plans to establish 7,056 new household connections to mingrids in selected areas in Uganda within four years</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Foundation Rural Energy Services (FRES) was set up to accelerate rural electrification in Sub-Saharan Africa. FRES&apos; vision is that rural electrification leaves no one behind.The main goal of the project, under SDG7 Results facility, is to establish new household connections to mini-grids in selected areas in Mali.</narrative>
  </description>
